.TH NOTM 1 "2026-08-24" "notm 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
notm \- native GTK4 client for Notmuch mail stores
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B notm
.RB [ --config
.IR path ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B notm
is a desktop mail client for existing Notmuch mail stores.  It provides a
column-based GTK4 interface with saved searches, Notmuch query search,
tag-based message actions, compose/reply/forward flows, local drafts, optional
sanitized visual HTML, and keyboard navigation.
.PP
Normal search, view, tag, fixture indexing, and configured sent/draft indexing
use
.B libnotmuch
directly rather than shelling out to the
.BR notmuch (1)
command-line client.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Read configuration from
.I path
instead of the default application configuration described under
.BR FILES .
.SH NORMAL OPERATION
.TP
.B launch
Start the GTK application for normal desktop mail use.
.TP
.BI "launch " MAILTO_URI
Open an RFC 6068
.B mailto
URI in an editable composer.  Recipient,
.BR Cc ,
.BR Bcc ,
subject, and plain-text body values are imported; unsupported header fields are
ignored and the message is never sent automatically.  If notm is already
running, the request is routed to that instance.  Replacing unsaved composer
contents still requires confirmation.
.TP
.BI "launch --message-id " MESSAGE_ID
Start the GTK application with the normal startup search and select the specific
Notmuch message id.  If the message is not in the loaded startup page, fall back
to a direct id search.
.TP
.B print-config
Print the effective configuration as JSON after default discovery.  The test
harness token, send environment values and arguments, and configured sync
commands are redacted by default.
.TP
.B print-config --show-secrets
Print the effective configuration with secret-bearing values unredacted for
backward compatibility.  This is unsafe for logs or shared output; use it only
for deliberate private local inspection.
.TP
.B probe-send
Probe the configured external send transport without sending mail.  This is a
safe way to check send-command configuration and does not load a Notmuch
database.
.SH TESTING AND DEBUGGING
These commands and flags are for development, smoke testing, or automated
validation.  They are not needed for normal mail use.
.TP
.B launch --fixture
Start the GTK application against a disposable fixture mailbox.
.TP
.B launch --test-harness --test-harness-socket PATH --test-harness-token TOKEN
Start with the local developer test harness enabled.  This lets tests drive the
running GTK app through a local Unix socket.  See
.BR notm-test-harness (7).
.TP
.B fixture-smoke
Create a disposable fixture Notmuch database, run basic searches, and verify the
fake send transport contract.
.TP
.B live-readonly-smoke
Open the configured Notmuch database read-only and run the configured default
query.  This touches live user data only read-only.
.TP
.B live-self-send
Send exactly one unique self-test message through the configured transport and
wait briefly for it to appear in Notmuch.  This sends real mail and does not
force sync.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/notm/config.toml
Default application configuration.
.TP
.I ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/notm/
Private composer recovery, local named drafts, cached compose attachments, and
tag-undo history.
.TP
.I Notmuch configuration and database
Explicit notm fields take precedence; otherwise libnotmuch uses the standard
.BR NOTMUCH_CONFIG ,
.BR NOTMUCH_DATABASE ,
.B NOTMUCH_PROFILE,
XDG, profile, and legacy discovery rules.
.SH SAFETY
.B notm
does not run startup sync or automatic
.B "notmuch new"
with the default configuration.  Sync commands are gated by
.BR [sync].enabled ,
their command-specific
.B *_enabled
flag, and a nonblank
.B *_command
value.  On a non-fixture launch, a command runs at startup only when its
command-specific
.B *_on_startup
flag is also true.  Eligible receive and database-update commands run in that
order.  After the selected commands succeed, the current search is refreshed.
Each command runs as
.B sh -c
with a configurable timeout and the selected Notmuch context in its environment.
Fixture mode never runs configured external sync commands.  Archive, trash,
and spam are tag operations; they do not delete ordinary message files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notm-config (5),
.BR notm-test-harness (7),
.BR notmuch (1)
